@startuml resource-handoff-sequence
' The O(1) retained-resource handoff: a host obtains a dictionary resource
' from libdictenstein, hands the two words to llev_transducer_new (which
' retains, negotiates vt.dictionary.v1, and validates), and starts a query
' that captures an immutable snapshot resource. The cursor holds only the
' snapshot retain, so it outlives the transducer and the source handle while
' the source keeps mutating unblocked.
' Color: host application = trust-boundary tint #FFEBEE (#B71C1C);
'   libdictenstein/provider = #D5F5E3 (#2E7D32); liblevenshtein = #FADBD8;
'   VtResource handles = #DCEDC8 (#33691E) in notes.
' Source of truth: src/bindings.rs (Provider::from_borrowed/from_owned,
'   ResourceTransducer::query_utf8), src/ffi/index.rs (llev_transducer_new),
'   docs/verification/tla/AbiResourceLifecycle.tla (VT-LIFE-1..6).
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 14
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontColor #102027
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowThickness 2
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBorderColor #455A64
  LifeLineBorderColor #90A4AE
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  BorderColor #F9A825
}

title Resource handoff — retain, negotiate, capture one snapshot, outlive the source

participant "Host application" as Host #FFEBEE
participant "libdictenstein\n(provider)" as Ldict #D5F5E3
participant "liblevenshtein\nllev_* C ABI" as Llev #FADBD8

Host -> Ldict : construct + fill dictionary\n(ldict_* CRUD)
Host -> Ldict : ldict_dictionary_resource(dict)
Ldict --> Host : VtResource {context, vtable}\n(born owning one retain)
note right of Host #F1F8E9
  Handing the resource on is copying
  two machine words — <latex>\mathcal{O}(1)</latex>, no
  serialization (VT-ABI-3, VT-LIFE-4).
end note

Host -> Llev : llev_transducer_new(&resource,\nLLEV_ALGORITHM_STANDARD, &transducer)
activate Llev #FADBD8
Llev -> Ldict : retain(context)
Llev -> Ldict : query_interface("vt.dictionary.v1",\nminimum_version = 1, &vt)
Ldict --> Llev : Ok + dictionary vtable
Llev -> Llev : validate_base + validate_dictionary\n(struct_size, abi_version, reserved,\nrequired ops, value domain)
Llev --> Host : LLEV_STATUS_OK + LlevTransducer*
deactivate Llev
note right of Llev #FBE9E7
  On any validation failure the fresh
  retain is released before the error
  returns — no leak, no double release
  (UNSAFE_ABI_CONTRACTS.tsv row
  ffi-borrowed-resource-retain-validate-release).
end note

Host -> Llev : llev_transducer_query_utf8(transducer,\n"cat", 3, 2, TRAVERSAL, &cursor)
activate Llev #FADBD8
Llev -> Ldict : snapshot(context, &snapshot_resource)
Ldict --> Llev : Ok + immutable revision\n(a second retained resource)
Llev -> Ldict : root(snapshot_context, &root)
Ldict --> Llev : Ok + root node id
Llev --> Host : LLEV_STATUS_OK + LlevQueryCursor*
deactivate Llev
note right of Llev #FBE9E7
  Snapshot capture is <latex>\mathcal{O}(1)</latex> structural
  sharing; the cursor traverses this frozen
  revision only (VT-SNAP laws, wave-W3
  Rocq home CursorSnapshotSemantics.v).
end note

Host -> Ldict : keep mutating the source dictionary\n(insert / remove / compact / checkpoint)
note right of Ldict #E8F5E9
  Writers proceed unblocked: the cursor
  holds no lock, only the snapshot retain.
end note

Host -> Llev : llev_transducer_free(transducer)
Llev -> Ldict : release(context)  «source retain settled»
Host -> Llev : cursor keeps yielding batches\n(snapshot retain still live)
Host -> Llev : llev_query_cursor_free(cursor)
Llev -> Ldict : release(snapshot_context)\n«snapshot retain settled; ledger balances to zero»
@enduml
